The strict function space is the neighbourhood system of strict maps whose neighbourhoods are the nonempty step-function sets of finite lists of neighbourhood pairs. The master is the universe. It is nonempty because the constantly bottom map is strict, and it is the step-function set of the empty list. The intersection of two such neighbourhoods is the step-function set of the concatenated lists, and a nonempty witness contained in the intersection remains a witness. Every neighbourhood is contained in the universe.
